# 13F — Service → Process

This is where things get interesting.

systemd can tell us which process belongs to a service.

For a service, we can obtain information such as:

```text
MainPID
```

For example:

```bash
systemctl show nginx.service --property=MainPID
```

which might return:

```text
MainPID=235
```

Then Galaxy already has:

```text
ProcessIdentityMap
```

So we can do:

```text
systemd
   ↓
MainPID = 235
   ↓
ProcessIdentityMap
   ↓
pid:235@create_time
```

This is exactly why your identity-map work earlier was important.

